# Contacts — /api/contacts
#
# Run `dotnet run --project JsonApiPoc` first, then click the gutter icon next to a request.
# `###` separates requests; the text after it is the request name. "->" notes the expected outcome.
#
# Seed: 1 Jan Kowalski (Acme), 2 Maria Nowak (Acme), 3 Piotr Wisniewski (Globex),
#       4 Anna Zielinska (Initech), 5 Adam Kowalski (Initech).
# Custom fields on contacts: leadSource (text), newsletterOptIn (boolean).
#
# Writes accept only JSON:API resource documents (Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json); any
# other body media type draws a 415. Requests below mutate the local SQLite database.

@host = http://localhost:5031

### List contacts
GET {{host}}/api/contacts
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### With their company side-loaded (compound document: data + included)
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?include=company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sorted by last name, then first name (two Kowalskis in the seed -> Adam before Jan)
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?sort=lastName,firstName
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Mixed directions: last name ascending, tie broken by first name DESCENDING (-> Jan before Adam)
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?sort=lastName,-firstName
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Second page of 2 -> links.prev/next, meta.total
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?page[number]=2&page[size]=2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Page past the end -> 200 with empty data; links.last shows the real last page
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?page[number]=99
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Sparse fieldsets across both types: names only, and only the company's name
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?include=company&fields[contacts]=firstName,lastName,company&fields[companies]=name
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Single contact (note customFields in attributes and links.self on every resource)
GET {{host}}/api/contacts/2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Single contact with its company side-loaded
GET {{host}}/api/contacts/1?include=company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Missing contact -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/contacts/999
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Following the hypermedia links on relationships.company
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Related resource: the contact's company (links.related) -> the full company resource
GET {{host}}/api/contacts/2/company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Relationship linkage: just the identifier (links.self) -> { "type": "companies", "id": "1" }
GET {{host}}/api/contacts/1/relationships/company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### The related company, trimmed with a sparse fieldset
GET {{host}}/api/contacts/1/company?fields[companies]=name
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Relationship on a missing parent -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/contacts/999/relationships/company
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Query validation -> 400 problem details
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Unsupported sort field -> 400 (detail lists lastName, firstName, email)
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?sort=height
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unsupported include path -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?include=deals
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown query parameter -> 400 (strict validation)
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?foo=bar
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Bare page parameter -> 400 (the page family is reserved by the spec)
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?page=2
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unsupported page parameter -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?page[offset]=10
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Invalid page size -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?page[size]=0
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown field in a sparse fieldset -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?fields[contacts]=nonexistent
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

### Unknown resource type in a sparse fieldset -> 400
GET {{host}}/api/contacts?fields[gadgets]=name
Accept: application/vnd.api+json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Writes: JSON:API resource documents (Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json is
# the only accepted body media type). Attributes carry the contact's own fields;
# company travels as a relationship.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Flat JSON body -> 415 (this API accepts only JSON:API request bodies)
POST {{host}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Flat", "lastName": "Json", "companyId": 1 }

### Create a contact from a spec-shaped resource document -> 201 + Location matching links.self
POST {{host}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "attributes": {
      "firstName": "Ewa",
      "lastName": "Lewandowska",
      "email": "ewa@globex.example.com",
      "phone": "+48 600 300 200",
      "customFields": { "leadSource": "referral", "newsletterOptIn": true }
    },
    "relationships": {
      "company": { "data": { "type": "companies", "id": "2" } }
    }
  }
}

### Patch one attribute -> 204; missing attributes and relationships keep their current values
PATCH {{host}}/api/contacts/1
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "id": "1",
    "attributes": { "email": "jan.kowalski@acme.example.com" }
  }
}

### Move the contact to another company through the relationships member -> 204
PATCH {{host}}/api/contacts/1
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "id": "1",
    "relationships": {
      "company": { "data": { "type": "companies", "id": "3" } }
    }
  }
}

### Company is required, so null linkage -> 422 (a contact always belongs to a company)
PATCH {{host}}/api/contacts/1
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "id": "1",
    "relationships": {
      "company": { "data": null }
    }
  }
}

### Client-generated id -> 403 (this server assigns ids)
POST {{host}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "id": "424242",
    "attributes": { "firstName": "Client", "lastName": "PickedTheId" },
    "relationships": {
      "company": { "data": { "type": "companies", "id": "1" } }
    }
  }
}

### Wrong resource type for this collection -> 409
POST {{host}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "deals",
    "attributes": { "title": "Wrong collection" }
  }
}

### Missing required attributes -> 422
POST {{host}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "attributes": { "email": "nobody@example.com" },
    "relationships": {
      "company": { "data": { "type": "companies", "id": "1" } }
    }
  }
}

### Unknown custom field -> 422
POST {{host}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "attributes": {
      "firstName": "Bad",
      "lastName": "Field",
      "customFields": { "nonexistent": 1 }
    },
    "relationships": {
      "company": { "data": { "type": "companies", "id": "1" } }
    }
  }
}

### Relationship pointing at a missing company -> 404
POST {{host}}/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "attributes": { "firstName": "Orphan", "lastName": "Contact" },
    "relationships": {
      "company": { "data": { "type": "companies", "id": "999" } }
    }
  }
}

### Update a missing contact -> 404
PATCH {{host}}/api/contacts/999
Content-Type: application/vnd.api+json

{
  "data": {
    "type": "contacts",
    "id": "999",
    "attributes": { "firstName": "Ghost" }
  }
}

### Delete a contact (deals/activities referencing it get their contact set to null) -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/contacts/5

### Delete a missing contact -> 404
DELETE {{host}}/api/contacts/999
